  "declaredIdentity": "tenant/controls/controlId; controlId derives tenant+program+normalized identifier. Create stores creation requestId+initial content and distinguishes changed intent. Later Review/Approve/Retire/periodic commands do not generally retain request intent; content revision differs from physical stream revision.",
  "invariant": "Only the exact current draft or retirement can be independently reviewed then activated, and accepted successor/retirement changes one control version line without overlapping effective intervals. Responsibilities cannot create unwaived conflicts with decisions already made on the exact revision.",
  "boundaryDecision": "narrow",
  "boundaryRationale": "Splitting draft review/approval from the current target or conflicting responsibilities would break the exact accepted review and historical SoD invariant. Keep that narrow decision context atomic; approved versions, old scopes, and full decision/retirement histories can be read-side records.",
